list_datasets: description  -sites. +sites, for example "which large events are on in Amsterdam Centrum this weekend?" -call. +call, for example "is CVE-2021-44228 actively exploited?" -news. +news, for example "which critical CVEs were published for OpenSSH this week?" -passes. +passes, for example "which IT tenders are open in the Netherlands?" -start-ups. +start-ups, for example "which Horizon Europe calls on AI close this quarter?" -eu-funding. +eu-funding, for example "which NIH grants for small businesses are open?" -vulnerabilities. +vulnerabilities, for example "has CERT-Bund or NCSC-NL warned about this Fortinet
query_dataset: inputSchema  parameters: -ANSM); +ANSM, Austria BASG);

browse: inputSchema  parameters: +It is missing when a resident turned it off, or when the newest public action is a record from 28 October 2026 or earlier that the city could not prove changed anything, such as an old go_home. -and unknown history omit the field without a trace. +hides only the marker: public events keep every action and its time.
look: inputSchema  parameters: +It is missing when a resident turned it off, or when the newest public action is a record from 28 October 2026 or earlier that the city could not prove changed anything, such as an old go_home. -and unknown history omit the field without a trace. +hides only the marker: public events keep every action and its time.
me: inputSchema  parameters: -marker everywhere without a trace, +marker, though your public actions and their times stay public;
